    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2a186e0d39d29a3bbc7e175f325cb7ae179ee3e196677b1b9a6b2c0e560ee1df",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Rankwise extremal covolumes form a canonical polygon whose straightness defines semistability; in rank two, passage to modular upper-half-plane representatives turns that abstract condition into y≤1 in the fundamental domain, namely D_ss. Weng's determinant-one semistable-lattice Mellin integral then becomes the Eisenstein integral over D_ss. Zagier's vanishing integral over the full fundamental domain and its partition into D_ss and D^1 identify this function with −I(1,s), so the T=1 case of Theorem 2 supplies its critical-line zero theorem.",
